# demo-celebrity-face-match's own recipe ships an always-on
# demo-celebrity-face-match.service and, via SYSTEMD_AUTO_ENABLE, a
# 98-demo-celebrity-face-match.preset that enables it. When demo-loop is
# installed the loop is meant to be the sole autostart -- it launches
# facematch itself as one of its slots -- so an independently running
# service instance just sits on /dev/video0 forever and every camera slot
# the loop then starts (facematch and object-detection alike) dies with
# "setup-pipeline-csi1 ... returned non-zero exit status 1" and a kernel
# "mipi_csis_set_fmt, set sensor format fail".
#
# 50- sorts before 98-, and systemd's first matching preset line wins, so
# this deterministically beats that recipe's enable regardless of the order
# the two packages' postinsts happen to run in.
disable demo-celebrity-face-match.service
